From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin <robinei@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:11:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/dsi: Disable DSI error recovery actions on VLV/CHV

EXPERIMENT, not for upstream until tested.

MIPI_EOT_DISABLE bits 2-7 disable the DSI controller's automatic
recovery actions (VLV PRM vol 10, MIPI_EOT_DISABLE): for an HS TX
timeout the controller otherwise ends HS mode with EOT and puts the
lanes in stop state; similar actions exist for LP RX timeout, high/low
contention, unrecognised data type and multi-bit ECC errors. i915 leaves
all of them enabled; Intel's Android ADF driver set them from the VBT.

On a GPD Win 1 (CHV, DSI video mode) the picture intermittently loses
alignment (one-frame pipe stall, DPI FIFO underrun, sometimes a lasting
byte-offset split). Disable the recovery actions to see whether one of
them is involved. Test together with the HS_TX_TIMEOUT u16 fix.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
index 877eab7..a95f6ca 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
@@ -1372,6 +1372,19 @@ static void intel_dsi_prepare(struct intel_encoder *encoder,
 	if (intel_dsi->clock_stop)
 		tmp |= CLOCKSTOP;
 
+	/*
+	 * EXPERIMENT: disable the DSI controller's automatic error recovery
+	 * actions (EOT + stop state on HS TX timeout, contention, ECC and
+	 * type errors), as Intel's Android ADF driver does from the VBT.
+	 */
+	if (display->platform.valleyview || display->platform.cherryview)
+		tmp |= LP_RX_TIMEOUT_ERROR_RECOVERY_DISABLE |
+			HS_RX_TIMEOUT_ERROR_RECOVERY_DISABLE |
+			LOW_CONTENTION_RECOVERY_DISABLE |
+			HIGH_CONTENTION_RECOVERY_DISABLE |
+			TXDSI_TYPE_NOT_RECOGNISED_ERROR_RECOVERY_DISABLE |
+			TXECC_MULTIBIT_ERROR_RECOVERY_DISABLE;
+
 	if (display->platform.geminilake || display->platform.broxton) {
 		tmp |= BXT_DPHY_DEFEATURE_EN;
 		if (!is_cmd_mode(intel_dsi))
